      "name": null,
      "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(3,-12)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=f(\\frac{1}{6}x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The function $y=f(\\frac{1}{6}x)$ represents a stretch of the function $y=f(x)$ by a factor of $6$ parallel to the $x$-axis. This has the effect of multiplying the $x$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the point $(3,-12)$ on $f(x)$ is mapped to the point $(6\\cdot 3,-12)=(18,-12),$ and this point must lie on the graph of $y=f(\\frac{1}{6}x).$",
